Input: {"question": "Who is Henrietta Maria O'Donel White Culpeper's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 202, "text": "As the sun set over the rolling hills of the Culpeper estate, Henrietta Maria O'Donel White Culpeper gazed out the window of her ancestral home, her mind wandering to the man who had captured her heart."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 203, "end": 352, "text": "It was a chilly autumn evening in 1915, and the world was at war, but in this quiet corner of England, Henrietta felt a sense of peace wash over her."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 353, "end": 508, "text": "She was lost in thought, her fingers absently tracing the intricate patterns on the antique lace tablecloth, when the sound of horse hooves echoed outside."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 509, "end": 616, "text": "The door burst open, and a tall, dark-haired man strode in, his eyes crinkling at the corners as he smiled."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 617, "end": 730, "text": "\"My apologies for the interruption, my dear,\" Christopher Barton said, as he handed her a bouquet of wildflowers."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 731, "end": 776, "text": "\"I couldn't resist the urge to surprise you.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 777, "end": 956, "text": "Henrietta's heart skipped a beat as she took in the sight of her husband, his worn leather boots and dusty riding coat a testament to the long ride he had undertaken to reach her."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 957, "end": 1127, "text": "She felt a flutter in her chest as he leaned in to kiss her, the scent of fresh air and horse sweat mingling with the subtle hint of cigar smoke that clung to his jacket."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1128, "end": 1332, "text": "As they sat together on the worn velvet sofa, sipping tea and watching the stars twinkle to life outside, Henrietta couldn't help but feel grateful for the chance encounter that had brought them together."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1333, "end": 1504, "text": "It was a meeting that had seemed improbable, given their vastly different backgrounds – she, a member of the landed gentry, and he, a rising star in the world of politics."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1505, "end": 1611, "text": "Yet, as they laughed and talked, their differences melted away, replaced by a deep and abiding connection."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1612, "end": 1886, "text": "In the years that followed, Henrietta would often look back on that autumn evening, remembering the way Christopher's eyes had sparkled as he spoke of his dreams for a united Europe, and the way her heart had swelled with pride as he shared his vision for a brighter future."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1887, "end": 1987, "text": "It was a future that, even in the midst of war, seemed within reach, as long as they stood together."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1988, "end": 2114, "text": "As the clock struck midnight, Christopher rose to leave, his duties in the Prime Minister's Office calling him back to London."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2115, "end": 2260, "text": "Henrietta walked him to the door, her hand nestled in the crook of his elbow, feeling the weight of their love and the promise of a new tomorrow."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 46, "text": "\"The Tides of Fate: A Tale of Love and Legacy\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 48, "end": 225, "text": "In the midst of the 19th century, when the British Empire was at its zenith, two individuals from different walks of life found themselves bound together by the threads of fate."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 226, "end": 439, "text": "Henrietta Maria O'Donel White Culpeper, a woman of elegance and refinement, and Louis Symonds Tindal, a dashing British Royal Navy officer, embarked on a journey that would forever alter the course of their lives."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 440, "end": 522, "text": "The year was 1835, and the winds of change were sweeping across the British Isles."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 523, "end": 613, "text": "The Industrial Revolution was in full swing, and the Empire's naval prowess was unmatched."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 614, "end": 763, "text": "It was against this backdrop that Louis Symonds Tindal, a young and ambitious officer, found himself stationed in the bustling port city of Plymouth."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 764, "end": 873, "text": "With a keen sense of duty and a thirst for adventure, Tindal was making a name for himself in the Royal Navy."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 874, "end": 1000, "text": "Meanwhile, in the picturesque countryside of Kent, Henrietta Maria O'Donel White Culpeper was living a life of quiet elegance."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1001, "end": 1149, "text": "Born into a family of modest means, Henrietta's beauty, intelligence, and strong will had earned her a reputation as a catch among the local gentry."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1150, "end": 1240, "text": "However, it was not until she met Louis Symonds Tindal that her life took a dramatic turn."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1241, "end": 1390, "text": "The exact circumstances of their meeting are lost to the annals of time, but it is clear that the two were drawn to each other like moths to a flame."}, "